ions. In addition, it offers cards and payments, including debit and credit cards, ATM and micro-ATM, UPI/Scan and Pay, fund transfer, doorstep banking, international payments, bill pay, mobile recharge, FASTag, and tax payments; AU 0101 and AU 0101 Business applications; and wealth products comprising mutual funds, ASBA/IPO, PMS/AIF/Bonds, and 3-in-1 trading and demat accounts. Further, the company provides life, health, and general insurance; and locker products. It serves urban, semi-urban, and rural markets, as well as salaried and self-employed individuals, small businesses, merchants, women entrepreneurs, farmers, micro-enterprises, and emerging affluent households. The company was formerly known as AU Financiers (India) Limited and changed its name to AU Small Finance Bank Limited in May 2017. AU Small Finance Bank Limited was incorporated in 1996 and is headquartered in Mumbai, India.","beta":0.608,"sharesOutstanding":749415850,"marketCap":724685160448,"trailingPE":23.195,"forwardPE":16.1312,"priceToBook":3.3242,"dividendYield":0.1,"heldPercentInsiders":0.3139,"heldPercentInstitutions":0.4973,"earningsGrowth":0.511,"revenueGrowth":0.36,"website":"https://www.au.bank.in","fullTimeEmployees":59207,"recommendationKey":"buy","targetMeanPrice":1090.9656,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":29,"financialCurrency":"INR"},"estimates":{"eps":{"0q":{"avg":11.605,"low":11.39,"high":11.82,"yearAgoEps":8.87,"numberOfAnalysts":2.0,"growth":0.3083,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1q":{"avg":null,"low":null,"high":null,"yearAgoEps":null,"numberOfAnalysts":null,"growth":null,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"0y":{"avg":47.6785,"low":44.6,"high":52.3,"yearAgoEps":35.01,"numberOfAnalysts":23.0,"growth":0.3619,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"},"+1y":{"avg":59.9458,"low":59.9458,"high":68.9,"yearAgoEps":47.795,"numberOfAnalysts":26.0,"growth":0.2542,"currency":"INR","methodology":"normalized"}},"revenue":{"0q":{"avg":37534618000.0,"low":37369236000.0,"h